  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 512a72de08c75cf4e8a8424f7b75a271, type: 3}
  m_Name: D6T2_BossParrotFishTalk_Dialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  npc: 33
  sequence:
  - dialogueText: Look at that, a quiet room. Magic, isn't it? Now, grab the mop.
      We need to scrub this place before our guest docks.
    buttonText: Cleaned it yesterday
  - dialogueText: Yesterday? Yesterday is at the bottom of the sea. Look at this
      floor... A parrotfish must have crawled inside.
    buttonText: Nonsense again?
  - dialogueText: Nonsense? It's science! Those colorful bastards chew on coral and
      rocks all day, crunching it down in their bellies
    buttonText: Fascinating. And then?
  - dialogueText: Then? They poop it out! Pure, fine, white sand. A big one can dump
      hundreds of kilos a year. Look at my floor!
    buttonText: It's just dust
  - dialogueText: It's parrotfish business, I tell you! And I won't have my Tavern
      looking like a tropical beach. Go get the bucket.
    buttonText: Mopping the beach...
